## 4. `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — Split Model Shard Resolution

**Responsibilities:** Resolves the shard paths of a split GGUF model from any shard's filename, validates that all shards exist, and returns them in order. Throws on missing shards.

**Proposed change:** The current implementation uses `std::ifstream(p, std::ios::binary)` to check file existence, which opens and immediately closes the file. On network filesystems or with many shards, this is slow. Replace with a platform-specific `stat`/`GetFileAttributes` call that does not open the file.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@ -1,5 +1,12 @@
 #pragma once

 #include <cstdio>
 #include <fstream>
 #include <stdexcept>
 #include <string>
 #include <vector>
+#ifdef _WIN32
+#include <windows.h>
+#else
+#include <sys/stat.h>
+#endif
@@ -1,6 +1,10 @@
     for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {
         char num[8];
         std::snprintf(num, sizeof num, "%05d", i);
         std::string p = any;
         p.replace(at - 5, 5, num);
-        if (!std::ifstream(p, std::ios::binary))
+        bool exists = false;
+#ifdef _WIN32
+        exists = GetFileAttributesA(p.c_str()) != INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES;
+#else
+        struct stat st;
+        exists = stat(p.c_str(), &st) == 0 && S_ISREG(st.st_mode);
+#endif
+        if (!exists)
             throw std::runtime_error("missing model shard " + p + " (shard " + std::to_string(i) + " of " +
                                      std::to_string(n) + "; is the download complete?)");
         out.push_back(std::move(p));
     }
```

**Verification cases:**
1. Run `gguf_split_test` and confirm it still throws on a missing shard and returns the correct ordered list for a valid 4-shard model.
2. On Linux, create a directory with a symlink named `model-00001-of-00002.gguf` pointing to a real file and confirm `gguf_split_paths` resolves it (the `stat` follows symlinks by default).

