## 7. `include/strata/core/conversation_memory.hpp` — Host Memory Telemetry

**Responsibilities:** Provides `conversation_available_memory()` (platform-specific: `GlobalMemoryStatusEx` on Windows, `MemAvailable` on Linux) and `conversation_mem_available()` (parses `/proc/meminfo` from an istream). Used by the conversation cache to decide whether parking is safe.

**Proposed change:** `conversation_mem_available` parses `/proc/meminfo` by searching for `"MemAvailable:"`. If the file contains `"MemAvailable_KB:"` (a hypothetical future kernel variant), the substring match would succeed but the value would be wrong. Anchor the match to the start of the line and require a space after the colon.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/core/conversation_memory.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/core/conversation_memory.hpp
@@ -1,6 +1,10 @@
 std::optional<uint64_t> conversation_mem_available(std::istream& meminfo) {
     std::string line;
     while (std::getline(meminfo, line)) {
-        if (line.find("MemAvailable:") == 0) {
+        if (line.size() > 13 && line.compare(0, 13, "MemAvailable:") == 0 && line[13] == ' ') {
             const char* p = line.c_str() + 13;
             while (*p == ' ') ++p;
             uint64_t kb = 0;
             while (*p >= '0' && *p <= '9') { kb = kb * 10 + (*p - '0'); ++p; }
             return kb * 1024;
         }
     }
     return {};
 }
```
